From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 20:19:40 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] sched/fair: Never pick the misfit task as its own rotation
 partner

misfit_rotate_work() checks that p is still on src_cpu, then scans the
bigger CPUs' rq->curr without locks. Load balancing can pull the misfit
task p onto an idle bigger CPU in between, so the scan can return p
itself. migrate_swap(p, p) then runs migrate_swap_stop() on dst_cpu,
which takes double_raw_spinlock(&p->pi_lock, &p->pi_lock) with IRQs off
and spins forever, while src_cpu spins in multi_cpu_stop().

Seen on m4.120: CPU 5 stopped answering IPIs and the NMI backtrace, RCU
stalled, the misfit_rotate_mutex owner sat in stop_two_cpus(), and the
desktop froze until a hard reboot.

Skip p when scanning for a partner.

Fixes: 2d24fbce39a3 ("sched/fair: Rotate misfit tasks with tasks on busy bigger CPUs")
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: LLM
(cherry picked from commit 294b3066364fe56bb10b1d306488002306d73b42)
---
 kernel/sched/fair.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/kernel/sched/fair.c b/kernel/sched/fair.c
index 270d8f3437..28450a1458 100644
--- a/kernel/sched/fair.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/fair.c
@@ -14902,7 +14902,11 @@ static void misfit_rotate_work(struct work_struct *work)
 			continue;
 
 		c = rcu_dereference_all(rq->curr);
-		if (!misfit_rotate_candidate(c) ||
+		/*
+		 * Balancing may have pulled p here since the check above;
+		 * migrate_swap(p, p) takes p->pi_lock twice in the stopper.
+		 */
+		if (c == p || !misfit_rotate_candidate(c) ||
 		    !cpumask_test_cpu(src_cpu, c->cpus_ptr))
 			continue;
 
